    "body": "### Problem\n\nTraditionally, the ruler in the last line is one cell shorter than in the statusline, in order to leave the last cell of the screen blank. I believe that the idea was to have both ruler positions aligned on the left for aesthetic reasons, which IMHO is not a good enough reason for the inconsistent widths, especially because they're not shown at the same time.\n\nThis used to work because the default ruler contains expanding whitespace, i.e. the equivalent of a top-level `%=`. And it works currently because the defaults in both positions are implemented by different means. But in general, a 'rulerformat' expression will naturally create a ruler of the same length, no matter where it is displayed. This becomes particularly inconvenient when trying to recover the old default behaviour while replacing the C implementation with a default 'rulerformat' expression that is used in both places.\n\nAccording to code comments, the reason for the empty cell at the end of the last line is to prevent unwanted \"scrolling\" on \"some terminals\"[^1]. I've never seen any other TUI deal with this problem.\n\nIn vim 3.0, the oldest version I could find on vim.org, the empty cell was guaranteed in a central function for putting a character on the screen: `screen_char`, with a similarly vague comment. Today, in Neovim, there are at least two features that currently don't respect this: ui2 and the statusline when `cmdheight=0`.\n\nThe only concrete information that I was able to find about this issue is a comment in Berkeley vi's `vs_modeline` function which shows the current mode at the (almost) end of the last line[^2]:\n```\n* Leave the last character blank, in case it's a really dumb terminal\n* with hardware scroll.  Second, don't paint the last character in the\n* screen, SunOS 4.1.1 and Ultrix 4.2 curses won't let you.\n```\nUnless I'm missing something, this workaround from the last century doesn't seem relevant nowadays.\n\n[^1]: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/v0.12.4/src/nvim/statusline.c#L310\n      https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/v0.12.4/src/nvim/statusline.c#L514\n[^2]: https://github.com/ghosthamlet/nvi/blob/nvi-1.81.6/vi/vs_refresh.c#L767\n      https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/n/nvi/nvi_1.81.6.orig.tar.gz\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInstead of adding the workaround in all places where it's currently missing: \n- extend the ruler in the last line all the way to the right edge of the screen, making the new default 18 cells, just like in the statusline (the exact same amount of place will be available to the rest of the UI as before)\n- the main work is to adapt about 50 test asserts, which saves work later for the final switch to ui2\n- get early feedback on master/nightly to see if it creates problems\n- if the repercussions are too great, move the ruler in the last line one cell to the left instead of shortening it again, but consider making this opt-in in the future",
